# スライドの描画の速さを、同じ実行の中で比べる (design 11.11), for tools/ui_run.py:
# the links of 仮身サンプル shown as slides by the slides of the process (open) and
# by the desktop's own (kslide, a UITEST command) in turn, three times each, so that
# both are measured under the same load of the machine. Each time the pages 1 to 8
# are turned twice; the lines slide: drew N in US us and slide: input to screen US us
# of the second turn are what is compared. A line slide: mode ... says which is which.
run /boot/SVCPROG.ELF 45 10000
expectin 60 svcprog: tvrtt fn_dra_txt width ns
apps 019a4370-3819-79a2-9758-881e1e0de90a basic-slide
logmark
open 019a4370-3819-79a2-9758-881e1e0de90a
expectsincein 60 slide: drew 1 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 2 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 3 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 4 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 5 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 6 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 7 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 8 in
logmark
key 4A
expectsince slide: drew 1 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 2 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 3 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 4 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 5 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 6 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 7 in
logmark
key 4F
expectsince slide: drew 8 in
logmark
key 4A
expectsince slide: drew 1 in
key 29
expect slide: closed
wait 500
logmark
kslide 019a4370-3819-79a2-9758-881e1e0de90a
expectsincein 60 slide: drew 1 in
